WEBVTT

00:29:59.954 --> 00:30:05.454
Is that basically right, that there is
ultimately no safe sort of space where

00:30:05.454 --> 00:30:07.538
we can say, oh, but that would
never be able to do that

00:30:07.788 --> 00:30:13.579
on a very long time horizon? I agree with
you, but that's such a long time horizon.

00:30:13.579 --> 00:30:17.913
I think that, you know, like maybe
we've merged by that point,

00:30:17.913 --> 00:30:21.204
like maybe we're all plugged
in and then, like,

00:30:21.204 --> 00:30:23.079
we're this sort of symbiotic thing.

00:30:24.329 --> 00:30:26.371
Like, I think there's an
interesting example,

00:30:26.371 --> 00:30:28.204
as we were talking about
a few minutes ago,

00:30:28.496 --> 00:30:32.788
where right now we have these systems that
have sort of enormous horsepower